==========
psion/opl #2822, from hzk, 3601 chars, May 6 13:20 96
Comment to 2817.
----------
I wrote a single line editor for my packet radio program a while back.
This used monospaced text, so I have modified it for proportional text.
The result is below!

Basically you can move the cursor around inside the text, and delete
and insert characters at will.  On the following extract there is no
check on whether the text goes off the display - my original program
sent the text to the transmitter before this could happen.

There may be the odd bug - I have not fully checked this proportional
text version.  Hopefully the cursor keeps in the correct place as you
type and delete - it seems OK.

You can add extras easily, like make the "Esc" key abort the action.
I also did a two line version for a series 3, and a whole page editor
(absolute nightmare)!  I threw away the code for the latter, since it
became impossible to understand after I blinked.

It may not be quite what you want, and there is bound to be something
in the Psion ROM to make it easier, but this OPL uses standard commands
which are all in the manual.  It may be possible to simplify and tidy
up the code too, especially around the code which manipulates the
cursor inside the text.

Anyway, here it is.  Hope it is some use.

Roger.


PROC main:

  GLOBAL pos%         REM number of characters from right end
  GLOBAL text$(80)    REM holds string
  LOCAL k%            REM key pressed
  gFONT 7             REM a suitable font
  gTMODE 3            REM replace mode
  gAT 0,100           REM start position

  DO                  REM get keys pressed
    k%=GET
  UNTIL sle%:(k%)=-1

  gAT 0,120 :gPRINT text$   REM print final text
  GET

ENDP


PROC sle%:(j%)
  LOCAL txtlen%          REM length of text$
  LOCAL charwid%         REM width of character

  charwid%=gTWIDTH(CHR$(j%))  REM get width of key pressed
  txtlen%=LEN(text$)
  CURSOR 1               REM cursor visible in default win

  IF j%=8                REM Delete pressed

    IF pos%=txtlen%      REM if cursor at start of text

      BEEP 2,500         REM nowt to delete!

    ELSEIF pos%<>0       REM if cursor inside text

      text$=LEFT$(text$,txtlen%-(pos%+1))+RIGHT$(text$,pos%)
      charwid%=gTWIDTH(MID$(text$,txtlen%-(pos%),1))
      gAT 0,100 :gPRINTB text$,gTWIDTH(text$)+charwid%
      gAT gTWIDTH(LEFT$(text$,txtlen%-(pos%+1))),gY

    ELSE                 REM if cursor at end od text

      charwid%=gTWIDTH(RIGHT$(text$,1))
      text$=LEFT$(text$,txtlen%-1)
      gAT 0,100 :gPRINTB text$,gTWIDTH(text$)+charwid%
      gAT gTWIDTH(text$),gY

    ENDIF

  ELSEIF j%=258   REM right arrow key pressed

    IF pos%>0

      pos%=pos%-1
      charwid%=gTWIDTH(MID$(text$,txtlen%-pos%,1))
      gAT gX+charwid%,gY

    ENDIF

  ELSEIF j%=259  REM left arrow key pressed

    IF gX<>0     REM cursor not at start of text

      charwid%=gTWIDTH(MID$(text$,txtlen%-pos%,1))
      gAT gX-charwid%,gY
      pos%=pos%+1

    ENDIF

  ELSEIF j%=262   REM "Home" key pressed

    gAT 0,100
    pos%=LEN(text$)

  ELSEIF j%=263  REM "End" key pressed

    gAT gTWIDTH(text$),gY
    pos%=0

  ELSEIF j%<>13 AND j%<256   REM a letter key pressed

    IF pos%=0   REM cursor at end of line

      text$=text$+CHR$(j%)
      gPRINT CHR$(j%)

    ELSE

      txtlen%=LEN(text$)
      text$=LEFT$(text$,txtlen%-pos%)+CHR$(j%)+RIGHT$(text$,pos%)
      gAT 0,100 :gPRINT text$
      gAT gTWIDTH(LEFT$(text$,txtlen%-(pos%-1))),gY

    ENDIF

  ELSEIF j%=13      REM "Enter" pressed

    RETURN -1

  ENDIF

ENDP




